-- Earn your Passport: the Taster account, the new check-in, three challenges, monthly Passport Challenge stops, business gift
-- cards and the Vault (LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-01: "lock it"). Concept session with V; canon canon-ve-earn-your-passport,
-- playbook ve-pricing-points-passport. Records the decision; the build follows. Safe to run twice.
insert into public.knowledge_records (slug, title, category, subcategory, status, owner, always_load, load_priority, tags, version, created_by, updated_by, change_summary, body)
select 'canon-ve-earn-your-passport',
  'Vegans Explore: earn your Passport (the Taster account, three challenges, the new check-in, monthly Passport Challenge stops, business gift cards and the Vault) (LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-01)',
  'decisions', 'membership', 'active', 'sar', false, 50,
  array['vegans-explore','membership','passport','points','challenges','vault','businesses'], 1, 'v', 'v',
  'Locked by Sean ("lock it") after a panel session on free versus paid memberships.',
  jsonb_build_object(
    'why', 'Sean, 2026-11-01: "people can earn their membership... not for what they did in the past, but for what you''re doing right now." Of 221 real visitors in October only 9 were paying members and the rest left no way to reach them again. No free account that can take part comes back (2026-10-27 rule kept); comps stay ended.',
    'principle', 'Browsing stays free; taking part stays the $11 Passport, or a membership earned now by doing something for the community. Earned is not given: the Depot still cannot hand out memberships.',
    'taster_account', 'Giving a name and email makes a Taster account: it opens only the sampler Guide, the person''s challenges, check-ins while a challenge runs and their own link for the Connector. Everything else they see as signed out: no votes, posts, saves or points to spend. Finishing a challenge or paying the $11 turns the same account into a membership (one email, one account across every brand).',
    'sampler', 'A Taste of Vegans Explore: the free piece every Guide already shows (Nutrition B12, the Dairy Buttermilk swap, Hard Rock Stadium, the Fort Lauderdale airport, tip 1 of the Creator and Nonprofit Guides, the free restaurant check) plus what Vegans Explore is, walked through by the whole cast, the For the animals side included. Every page ends with "the rest of this Guide comes with your Passport." Its sign-up asks three questions (what brings you here, your city, where you are on your Vegan journey) that pick the suggested Guide and the chapter news. The Welcome Guide stays public.',
    'challenges', jsonb_build_array(
      'Support Local: check in at 3 Vegan places within 30 days, at least one thing from the check-in menu at each, and I bought something at least once. During a month with Passport Challenge stops, 3 of that month''s stops.',
      'The Connector: 3 people join with the $11 through your own link.',
      'The Advocate: one free event on the guest pass, a visit or volunteering at a sanctuary or rescue event, and one share from the Fosters or Rescues board.'),
    'challenge_rules', 'Pick 1 to 3; each has Start and 30 days to finish, with one restart. Every task is proven like a bounty (a photo, the phone''s location, a check-in at the door) and approved by the team before it counts. Each challenge is worth 1,100 points. One challenge: its points pay the Passport and the Taster becomes a member. All three: a member, the other 2,200 points to their balance, and Level 2 from lifetime points (3,300 plus 111 a referral). A badge on the profile (working name Trailblazer). Earned members get no extra welcome points beyond what the challenges paid.',
    'check_in', 'For everyone: after I''m here (150 m, as today) the screen asks What are you doing here today? What I ordered (a photo, the upload opens only while checked in there), I bought something (a receipt photo, card number covered), Post it (the link to an Instagram or TikTok post tagging the place and @vegansexplore), a shout-out (a positive prompt, read by a person before it shows), and the bounties open at that place. Photos also go to the restaurant (a BrandDesk client''s Library). Owners and staff earn nothing at their own place. Logan''s starting points, Sean''s to change: check-in 10, meal photo 15, receipt 25, post 25, shout-out 10, a cap per place per day.',
    'passport_challenge_stops', 'The monthly Passport Challenge becomes the event in every chapter: up to five featured Vegan businesses a month plus one free community stop (a sanctuary, rescue or nonprofit event). Slots open about six weeks ahead; the team approves and locks the five by the 10th of the month before; with more applicants than slots no business runs two months in a row, with fewer it may repeat; they go live on the 1st. The first check-in of the month at a stop pays the most, then less for each after (like first to confirm). Pilot: South Florida, then chapters as they reach five businesses.',
    'business_offer', 'A business pays for its slot in kind: four $25 digital gift cards ($100). It is offered as a Promotion in the Vegan Restaurant Guide and on /business: five slots a chapter, the deadline, the ask, why it is good marketing, and their card as it will look on a phone. Choosing it says: if you are not a member yet, your cards give you full membership, and your claim is included. They can back out there. The form is the agreement (typed name and I agree): promotional cards, $25 off, one per visit, no cash back, expiring 12 months after they are won, removed if the business closes, Florida law; the lawyer reads it once before the pilot. A business that takes a slot before January 1, 2027 is a Founding Member (paid in value). Sean prefers businesses come in this way over paying the $11.',
    'business_follow_up', 'The offer goes out with the business''s own tracked link; about 24 hours later, not opened or signed in: your slot is still open, with the deadline; opened but not chosen: what it really costs (about $30 in food) and how easy redeeming is; chosen: welcome, next steps, staff PIN set-up. From the team, never Sean''s name; anything left lands in the Inbox for a Community Manager.',
    'cards_and_redeeming', 'The member''s card lives in their dashboard: the restaurant''s name and logo, $25, the member''s name, a code and the expiry. Staff redeem with no app: the member shows the card and staff type the restaurant''s short staff PIN on the member''s phone; the code is used once on our side. The PIN changes when staff leave. The owner sees cards won and redeemed as counts, never names.',
    'vault', 'Un-tables the Vault (tabled 2026-10-31 with "members do not spend points at managed restaurants"). The month''s cards by city; members bid points for a week, the highest bid wins and only the winner''s points are taken; one win per member a month. A public Vault page shows every prize by city to anyone, bidding for members only. Cards nobody wins stay up until won or expired, so the business keeps its promotion.',
    'content_gig', 'A month ahead, one gig per stop on the Gig Board: a 15 to 30 second vertical clip of the owner ("We''re so excited to be...") and someone eating there, cut into a reel, with an example page showing the format; a creator, an Ambassador or the owner on the template can do it.',
    'points_rule_change', 'Changes the 2026-10-25 rule that points given to a business are "a boost, never money" (Sean''s sign-off: "lock it"). A business may spend the points it has received on our services (the Partner plan, BrandDesk, the shop, a Diplomat membership) at 1 cent a point, up to half the price, never cashed out. $25 off is 2,500 points. Members keep giving points to sanctuaries and businesses.',
    'not_ready_yet_emails', 'Tasters get Day 0 the sampler, Day 3 their city this week, Day 7 a story or episode that fits their answers, Day 14 the full Guide that matches, then the Daily Pulse weekly for their chapter; in December three notes on Founding Membership closing at midnight Eastern on January 1; after that the Passport. At most one a week outside December, one-click unsubscribe, clicks tracked by name; paying the $11 ends the track. London needs an unticked consent box. Reuse the outreach people-list engine.',
    'not_membership', 'A Taster is "on the list", never a member, and the email list is never a way into the community.',
    'build_order', 'Logan: 1. the new check-in menu (for everyone), 2. the business sign-up, agreement, cards, staff PIN and Vault for the South Florida pilot, 3. the Taster account and the sampler, 4. the three challenges, 5. the two-day business follow-up and the not-ready-yet emails, 6. the content gig, 7. the business points rule.',
    'playbook', 've-pricing-points-passport')
where not exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_records where slug = 'canon-ve-earn-your-passport');

-- The points rule change, recorded on the pricing canon too.
update public.knowledge_records
set body = body || jsonb_build_object('update_2026_11_01_business_points', 'Points a business receives may be spent on our services (Partner plan, BrandDesk, the shop, a Diplomat membership) at 1 cent a point, up to half the price, never cashed out (Sean, 2026-11-01, canon-ve-earn-your-passport). Earned memberships: one Earn your Passport challenge (1,100 points of approved tasks) is a membership; a business''s four $25 gift cards for a Passport Challenge slot are a membership paid in kind.'),
    version = version + 1, updated_at = now(), updated_by = 'v',
    change_summary = 'Business points on our services; earned memberships (canon-ve-earn-your-passport).'
where slug = 'canon-ve-guide-pricing' and not (body ? 'update_2026_11_01_business_points');

insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-pricing-points-passport', 'vegans-explore', 'V',
  $pb$LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-01 ("lock it"). EARN YOUR PASSPORT (canon canon-ve-earn-your-passport). Not built yet.
WHY. Free versus paid, run past a panel: browsing stays free, taking part stays the $11 Passport, no free account that can take part, comps stay ended, and a membership can be earned by what someone does now. Sean: "I actually would prefer people to do that than pay the $11."
1. THE TASTER ACCOUNT. Name and email make a Taster account: the sampler Guide, their challenges, check-ins while a challenge runs, their own link; the rest of the site as signed out. Finishing a challenge or paying the $11 makes the same account a membership.
2. THE SAMPLER, A Taste of Vegans Explore: every Guide's free piece plus what Vegans Explore is, walked through by the whole cast; three sign-up questions pick the suggested Guide and chapter news. The Welcome Guide stays public.
3. THREE CHALLENGES (pick 1 to 3, Start, 30 days, one restart; proven like bounties and approved): Support Local (3 check-ins at Vegan places, one action each, a receipt at least once; in a stops month, 3 of the month's stops), The Connector (3 people join with the $11 through your link), The Advocate (a free event on the guest pass, a sanctuary or rescue visit or volunteering, a Fosters or Rescues share). Each worth 1,100 points: one is a membership; all three a membership, 2,200 points on top and Level 2. A profile badge (working name Trailblazer).
4. THE NEW CHECK-IN, for everyone: What are you doing here today? What I ordered (photo only while checked in), I bought something (receipt), Post it (link), a shout-out (positive prompt, read first), bounties here. Owners and staff earn nothing at their own place. Starting points 10, 15, 25, 25, 10, capped per place per day.
5. MONTHLY PASSPORT CHALLENGE STOPS: up to five featured businesses a chapter a month plus one free community stop; slots open about six weeks ahead, locked by the 10th of the month before, no back-to-back when there is a waitlist, live on the 1st; first check-in pays the most. Pilot South Florida.
6. THE BUSINESS OFFER: four $25 digital gift cards for a slot, offered as a Promotion in the Vegan Restaurant Guide and on /business; it gives membership (Founding before January 1) and covers the claim; the form is the agreement (promotional, one per visit, no cash back, 12 months after won, removed if the business closes, Florida law; lawyer reads it once). Two-day follow-up on their tracked link: not opened, opened not chosen, chosen; from the team, leftovers to the Inbox.
7. CARDS AND THE VAULT: the card in the member's dashboard; staff redeem by typing the restaurant's short PIN on the member's phone, one use, PIN changed when staff leave; owners see counts only. The Vault is un-tabled: members bid points for a week, one win a month, only the winner pays; a public Vault page shows every prize by city; unwon cards stay up until won or expired.
8. THE CONTENT GIG a month ahead: a vertical owner clip and someone eating, cut into a reel, from an example format.
9. POINTS RULE CHANGE: a business may spend points it received on our services at 1 cent a point, up to half the price, never cashed out ($25 off is 2,500 points).
10. NOT-READY-YET EMAILS: Day 0, 3, 7, 14, then the weekly Daily Pulse; three December notes on the Founding deadline; London consent box; paying ends the track.
BUILD ORDER (Logan): the check-in menu; the business sign-up, agreement, cards, PIN and Vault for the South Florida pilot; the Taster account and sampler; the challenges; the follow-ups and emails; the content gig; the business points rule.$pb$,
  'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-pricing-points-passport' and body like 'LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-01 ("lock it"). EARN YOUR PASSPORT%');
